{
 "about": "Which models count as geospatial foundation models (GeoFMs) in the dataset-benchmarking analysis. A model is in scope if its workbook registry category is one of geofm_categories, or it is listed in geofm_uncategorised or geofm_from_baseline_pretrained (no registry category, but pretrained on Earth-observation data and offered as a reusable representation). Everything else is out of scope: generic vision models (ImageNet / CLIP / ADE20K), random initialisation, task architectures trained from scratch, classical / trivial / feature baselines, and paper-internal baselines or reproductions. Out-of-scope models would inflate spread and the shared signal of datasets whose comparisons include them.",
